# Known, accepted drift. Format:
#   <slug>|<substring of the drift message>   # why, and what the fix is
#
# Narrower than .lint-skip, which exempts a tool from every check. An entry
# here keeps the tool checked for everything else, so --strict can gate on new
# drift while this backlog is worked through.
#
# A waiver is a promise to come back, not a fix. Deleting a line should be the
# last step of fixing the thing it describes.

# ── Club colour sources (opened 30/07/2026) ──────────────────────────────────
# These six load club data outside the canon. Fixing each changes what the tool
# renders — clubs-data.js has 29 of 72 primaries drifted from clubs-meta — so
# each needs its own change and its own look before/after, not a blanket sweep.
graphics/table-graphic|stale clubs-data.js mirror        # 29 primaries wrong; needs per-tool verify
graphics/fixtures-results|direct clubs-meta URL          # fetches raw.githubusercontent; move to NL.clubs
graphics/league-tables|direct clubs-meta URL             # fetches raw.githubusercontent; move to NL.clubs
graphics/single-fixture|direct clubs-meta URL            # fetches raw.githubusercontent; move to NL.clubs
graphics/top-scorers|direct clubs-meta URL               # fetches raw.githubusercontent; move to NL.clubs
